## Code Example

```javascript
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold, timeout) {
    this.failures = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.timeout = timeout;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
    this.lastFailure = null;
  }

  recordFailure() {
    this.failures++;
    this.lastFailure = Date.now();
    if (this.failures >= this.threshold) {
      this.state = 'OPEN';
      setTimeout(() => this.state = 'HALF-OPEN', this.timeout);
    }
  }

  recordSuccess() {
    this.failures = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }

  canExecute() {
    return this.state !== 'OPEN';
  }
}
```

Why This Is Asked
Tests practical SRE handling of backlog storms in asynchronous, cross-region pipelines, beyond generic incident response. It emphasizes concrete controls, testability, and safe recovery.

Key Concepts
- Asynchronous pipelines (Kafka, event buses)
- DLQ and consumer lag signals
- Backpressure and throttling policies
- Idempotency and exactly-once semantics
- Canary testing and burst traffic in staging
- Observability: backlog, latency, error ratios, SLOs

Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo dynamic throttling for backlog-aware recovery
class ThrottleController {
  constructor(maxRate) { this.rate = maxRate; this.maxRate = maxRate; this.minRate = 0.1; }
  adjust(state) {
    if (state.backlog >= state.targetBacklog) this.rate = Math.max(this.minRate, this.rate * 0.8);
    else if (state.lag <= state.targetLag) this.rate = Math.min(this.maxRate, this.rate * 1.25);
    applyRate(state.topic, this.rate);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to handle external dependency fragility, multi-tenant isolation, and production risk management. The question evaluates end-to-end instrumentation, resilience patterns, and practical operational procedures rather than theoretical knowledge.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end observability with OpenTelemetry
